course: dictionary
lesson: 14457
title: Parchment: old writing and baking paper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Parchment is a material for writing on. Long ago, people made it from the thin, dried skin of a sheep, goat or calf. Context clues help you spot its meaning: look for words like scroll, old, ink or history.
explain: «The monks copied the story onto parchment by hand.» Monks copy books with a pen, and by hand means not by machine. So parchment must be the material they wrote on. An old document written on it is also called a parchment.
explain: Parchment can also mean thick, stiff, yellowish paper. «Mum lined the cake tin with parchment before she poured in the mixture.» Here it means baking paper, because it is used in cooking. The same word can mean old animal skin or paper for cakes, so check the sentence to see which fits.
fact: Parchment is made from thin, dried animal skin, usually from sheep, goats or calves.
fact: Parchment means a material for writing on, and also an old document written on it.
fact: The word «parchment» is used for the material itself, while «a parchment» means one document.
fact: In history, medieval books, charters and the Magna Carta (1215) were written on parchment.
fact: Parchment can also mean thick, stiff, yellowish paper, such as baking parchment used in cooking.
exercise: «The old map was drawn on parchment and rolled up tight.» What is parchment in this sentence? | A type of tree | A kind of cake | *A material made from dried animal skin | A metal box
exercise: «The White Rabbit unrolled a parchment scroll in Alice in Wonderland.» What did the White Rabbit unroll? | A window blind | A bag of sweets | A carpet | *A scroll, a document written on parchment
exercise: Mum says, «Line the tin with parchment before baking.» What is the parchment for? | *Stopping the cake from sticking | Keeping the cat warm | A treasure map | A letter to a friend
test: Which animals were the skins used to make parchment? | Pigs and horses | Cats and dogs | Fish and birds | *Sheep, goats and calves
test: Which of these was often written on parchment in medieval times? | Text messages | *Books and charters | Printed newspapers | Emails
exam: Pupil reads, «The old parchment crackled when I unrolled it.» What does old parchment most likely mean? | A kind of shiny sweet | A new cake tin | *A very old document written on animal skin | A sheet of printer paper
